# Apify API token — get yours at https://console.apify.com/account/integrations
APIFY_TOKEN=

# Anthropic API key — used by reddit:summarize to generate structured insights
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google Analytics 4 — set in Cloudflare Pages environment variables
PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# GA4 numeric property ID for ga4-pull.ts (Admin → Property Settings → Property ID, NOT the G-XXXXXXXX tag)
# The service account in credentials/gsc-service-account.json must be added to the GA4 property
# with Viewer role (GA4 Admin → Property Access Management) and the
# "Google Analytics Data API" must be enabled in Google Cloud Console.
GA4_PROPERTY_ID=

# DataForSEO credentials — required for keyword-discovery.ts
# Sign up at https://dataforseo.com/ and find API credentials in your dashboard
DATAFORSEO_USERNAME=
DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=
# Set to 'false' to use production API (costs money). Default: sandbox (free).
DATAFORSEO_SANDBOX=true


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# God's-Eye Nightly — L1 collectors (scripts/collectors/, PRD §7.4)
#
# `npm run collect:all` never fails on a missing key. Every variable below that
# is unset produces `healthy: false` with a reason naming the variable, which
# becomes a ledger finding that closes itself the night the key is supplied.
# So an empty value here is a tracked gap, not a crash — but it IS a gap.
#
# Nightly CI reads these from repo secrets; nightly.yml already passes them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- collectors/gsc.ts (requirement R6, URL Inspection) ---
# The full service-account JSON on ONE line. Locally you can instead leave this
# empty and keep credentials/gsc-service-account.json on disk; the collector
# prefers the env var and falls back to the file. In CI only the env var exists.
GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Optional. Caps how many indexable URLs get inspected per run (default: all 49).
# Any cap makes the collector report healthy:false with partial R6 coverage —
# that is intended, not a bug. Useful for a fast local smoke test.
GSC_INSPECT_LIMIT=

# --- collectors/clarity.ts ---
# Microsoft Clarity → Settings → Data Export. Also refreshes data/clarity/.
# The collector spends 1 of the 10 requests/day/project on a liveness ping.
CLARITY_TOKEN=

# --- collectors/cloudflare.ts (PRD §10.1 — the one blocking prerequisite) ---
# Create at Cloudflare → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token (custom):
#   Account → Cloudflare Pages : Read       (deployment id + build status)
#   Zone    → Analytics        : Read       (cache hit rate)
#   Zone    → Firewall Services: Read       (WAF events)
# Without it the collector reports: "CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN not set — see PRD §10.1"
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# All optional — auto-discovered from the token when omitted. Set them to skip
# the discovery calls or to disambiguate a multi-account / multi-project token.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_PAGES_PROJECT=

# --- collectors/quotas.ts ---
# SerpAPI (free tier: 250 searches/month).
SERP_API_KEY=
# Firecrawl (free tier: 500 pages/month).
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# DataForSEO reuses DATAFORSEO_USERNAME / DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD above.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CANONICAL NAMES — the A8 answer, in one place
#
# Two credentials have two spellings each. The names below are CANONICAL. They
# are canonical because they are the names the GitHub secrets actually have and
# the only ones any workflow passes:
#
#   nightly.yml           SERP_API_KEY · DATAFORSEO_USERNAME · DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD
#   monday.yml            DATAFORSEO_USERNAME · DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD
#   keywords-monthly.yml  DATAFORSEO_USERNAME · DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD
#
#   canonical              deprecated alias    who still accepts the alias
#   ---------------------  ------------------  --------------------------------
#   SERP_API_KEY           SERPAPI_KEY         scripts/collectors/quotas.ts only
#   DATAFORSEO_USERNAME    DATAFORSEO_LOGIN    scripts/collectors/quotas.ts only
#
# The aliases are the vendors' own documented names. quotas.ts resolves either,
# which is exactly why the drift stayed invisible for so long: a machine set up
# entirely under the vendor spellings passes the nightly quota check and then
# aborts in keyword-discovery.ts / keyword-gap-discovery.ts /
# competitor-intelligence.ts, none of which accept an alias.
#
# The aliases still work — nothing is being broken — but as of 2026-08-09 they
# are no longer silent. `npm run collect:all` prints an ENV NAME DRIFT block
# naming the variable and the rename, and records it (names only, never values)
# on data/collectors/latest.json. Definitions live in scripts/lib/env-names.ts;
# do not add a third spelling for anything.
#
# Renaming a GitHub secret is the one thing NOT to do casually here: Actions
# substitutes an empty string for a secret name that does not exist, so a typo
# in a rename fails silently and the collector just goes blind. That already
# happened once — see wiki/log.md, 2026-08-06.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- collectors/github-actions.ts ---
# No variable locally: it shells out to `gh`, which uses your keyring login.
# In CI, nightly.yml supplies GH_TOKEN from secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN.

# --- collectors/amazon.ts ---
# No variable, and never will be. Amazon Associates has no reporting API
# (PRD §4, §10.2). Drop the manual CSV export in raw/affiliate/YYYY-MM-DD-amazon-csv/;
# the collector nags once it is more than 7 days old.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SITE IDENTITY — scripts/lib/site.ts
#
# Both OPTIONAL and both default to this site. They exist so a fork does not have
# to patch code to stop impersonating tallchairadvisor.com in its own alerts.
#
# Every alarm this pipeline raises used to be site-blind: the ntfy push said
# `God's-Eye 2026-08-13 (88% coverage)` and the model prompt hardcoded the
# domain. With one site that is fine. With two, the lock screen shows two
# notifications identical but for a percentage — which answers neither of the
# questions being asked, "is my site broken" and "which one".
#
#   SITE_DOMAIN  full domain, used where there is room: the nightly model prompt.
#                Default: tallchairadvisor.com
#   SITE_LABEL   short name for the ntfy title and the report H1, where a
#                lock-screen preview is cut off around 30-40 characters.
#                Default: the first DNS label of SITE_DOMAIN (→ tallchairadvisor).
#                Set it explicitly when two sites share a first label —
#                tallchair.com and tallchair.io both derive `tallchair` and would
#                rebuild the exact ambiguity this exists to remove.
#
# Only nightly-report.ts reads these today. The other ~56 files in scripts/ that
# mention the domain keep their literals ON PURPOSE: extracting a general
# site.config.ts from a single example is inventing an abstraction against a
# sample size of one. The second site is what tells you which couplings hurt.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SITE_DOMAIN=
SITE_LABEL=
